    description: "FOUND 2026-10-04 while fixing WI-faful (branch jgstern-agent/fix/losod). With the declaration now defining its variable, `h := func() string { ... return v ... }` then `os.WriteFile(\"o.txt\", []byte(h()), 0o600)` still reads ddg_mixed / escaped, before and after the fix. Cause: the Go, TypeScript and Rust def/use extractors do not count the CALLEE of a plain call as a use (`foo(a)` uses a, not foo -- right for a declared function, wrong for a LOCAL variable holding a function). So `h` is defined at the declaration, never used, and unaccounted_names reports it (the walk escapes; it does not refute).\n\nRepro fixtures (verify-claims, claim host_secret -> host_fs): ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/losod/fx/go_func_literal, rs_closure, ts_arrow_decl -- all three read escaped in both arms. Java is not affected: `s.get()` reads `s` as a receiver.\n\nShape of a fix: a callee identifier that the SAME function defines as a local is a use. The extractors do not know the function's locals per statement, so this likely belongs in populate_def_use_for_cfg or in a per-function pass rather than per statement. Volume unmeasured."  # 4ef4
    fields: {}  # 4ef4
